[h1]Community Patch 1.0 and more[/h1]
Ten gameplay, fleet, logistics and interface modules in one DW2 Mod Launcher entry.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Cancellation Refunds[/b] — recover the unused share of the recorded state payment for a new unfinished ship, station, facility or troop order. Use the normal cancel action or Scuttle on an eligible unfinished hull.
[*][b]Colony Event Display Fix[/b] — refreshes grouped event tooltips as contributing colonies change.
[*][b]Colony Support Rules[/b] — residents under Exterminate incur 20% of their support share and generate no colony revenue or tax base.
[*][b]Deep Space Stability and Refuel[/b] — stable deep-space coordinates and two optional manual fleet refuelling orders.
[*][b]Freight Visibility[/b] — see cargo on board, planned pickups and foreign carriers in resource tooltips.
[*][b]HyperDeny on Move[/b] — keeps player HyperDeny available against enemies at war while following manual Move orders.
[*][b]Inherited Ship Retirement[/b] — applies Never enlistment to eligible ships inherited through last-colony conquest.
[*][b]Racial Research Unlock[/b] — unlocks frontier racial research after your colonies hold three billion residents of that race.
[*][b]Resource Intelligence[/b] — buy the location of an unknown resource deposit through diplomacy.
[*][b]Resource source pointers[/b] — hover the source count in Economy to point to surveyed deposits. The denominator counts discovered deposits.
[*][b]Resources stockpile and priorities[/b] — click a Stockpile amount to see the stores, cargo aboard, scheduled pickups and freighters assigned. Set delivery priority from 1 to 10 and optional caps by ship count or percentage of the fleet.
[*][b]Camera controls[/b] — open Esc → Settings → Camera to set separate galaxy and system wheel speeds, acceleration, smoothing, and focus for Show Me, the ship list and hotkeys. The Galaxy 3× / System 2× preset sets the two speeds together. Apply saves the choices to the active launcher profile.
[*][b]Salvage and Refit[/b] — select an owned ship or station carrying working equipment your empire has not researched. Open the removable-module icon beside Scuttle or in a free action slot. Choose a compatible design and confirm. Ships use a yard. A free automated constructor travels to a station, which keeps its orbit. Normal retrofit prices and local resource rules apply. Unfamiliar parts actually removed earn the ordinary ship-disassembly research reward.
[*][b]Station dismantling and recovery[/b] — confirm Dismantle entire station to remove its equipment and then the hull. Cancel before the hull is lost to keep earned research. Repair dismantled bays fits compatible researched parts where possible. The confirmation identifies bays with no replacement. Rebuilding a stripped bay gives no additional research. Orders and stripped bays persist across save/load.
[*][b]Retirement Research Report[/b] — lists every research boost awarded when your ship is disassembled at a base, including racial rewards. Each technology shows its actual gain. The report only displays what the game awarded.
[/list]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Open the Community Patch settings in DW2 Mod Launcher. Each of the ten modules has its own Enable switch and description. All start enabled. Restart the game to apply a change. Both tanker commands keep their saved values while the refuelling module is off.
Open [b]Esc > Settings > Camera[/b] to tune the camera while playing. Apply saves your choices for the mod manager and future sessions. Cancel discards your edits. Galaxy 3x / System 2x changes only the two map speeds. In the mod manager, select the preset to apply it once at game start.
[b]Camera[/b] gives Show Me and ship list focus separate choices. Choose Keep current zoom, System Map, Galaxy Map or Game default. The defaults are System Map for Show Me and Keep current zoom for ship focus.
[b]Zoom speed[/b] has independent settings for the system and galaxy views. Choose Game to use your regular game preference or set a fixed speed from 1x to 4x.
[b]Wheel acceleration[/b] raises the speed during quick wheel steps. Choose Off, 2x, 3x or 4x for the maximum speed. Slow scrolling uses your base speed.
[b]Wheel zoom smoothing[/b] offers Off, Short, Soft and Inertia. Short and Soft ease to the scale you chose. Inertia adds a little movement after fast scrolling. The default is Off.
[list]
[*][b]Keep gathering while refuelling[/b] preserves a manual fleet's Move destination when you then order it to refuel from its tankers.
[*][b]Gather and refuel here[/b] adds a rendezvous order to the manual fleet's map menu. It requires a tanker. Hold Shift to queue it. The next order waits for refuelling.
[/list]
Both options start off. Enable them in Mod Settings under Community Patch. Salvage and Refit also has its own switch in the launcher.

[h2]Requirements and load order[/h2]
Built for [b]Distant Worlds 2 Steam Beta 1.3.8.8[/b]. The pack checks the game assembly at startup. A later game build may require a new pack build. Automated checks covered package loading, saved orders, ship and station refits, station dismantling, repair after cancellation, and the action-panel icon.

Use Steam Beta 1.3.8.8 and DW2 Mod Launcher 1.0.44 or later. Subscribe to Positronic Matrix and load it before Community Patch. Place enabled companions ahead of Community Patch as shown in the launcher's dependency view. XL Galaxy Generation is a separate optional add-on for new campaigns.
Optional companions include Freighter Logistics, Ship Logistics, Galaxy Waypoints, Diplomatic Corps, Troop Logistics, War Chest and Coherent R&D.
If you use standalone Freight Dispatch, load it after Community Patch. Load Advanced Construction Mod after Freight Dispatch when using both.

To switch an existing campaign, save to a separate slot. Disable the individual module entries listed above, enable Community Patch, review the refuelling options and start through DW2 Mod Launcher. Load your separate save after confirming the pack initialized successfully.

[h2]Plans and gameplay testing[/h2]
Planned for investigation: let ordinary AI empires assess when studying unfamiliar parts and rebuilding to a compatible design would pay off. AI empires currently follow their usual retrofit rules. Possible AI use of waypoints when planning a war is a separate design idea.
Gameplay checks still open include a constructor's complete intersystem trip, the confirmation window at different UI scales, and camera feel with a physical wheel. Reports on these cases are welcome.

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Use this Workshop item's Discussions for bug reports and suggestions. Include the game build, Community Patch version, other enabled mods and steps that show the behaviour.
